  "version": "0.8.1-beta.1",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.8.0`\n\n### Features\n\n- reopen the tab closed last with Cmd+Shift+T on macOS (unbound elsewhere, where Ctrl+Shift+T opens a tab) or from the tab bar's menu: a tab of the bar comes back in its place with its split, its pane sizes and the pane that had the focus, every local shell in the directory it was in and every connection connecting again; a pane closed out of a split goes back exactly where it was while that tab is as it was left, else beside the pane it was next to, else as a tab of its own; the last 20 closings are kept for this run only, without the passwords typed for them, and pages and remote files are left out ([ad8cffaf](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/ad8cffaf4f6450231a47f2aac4f29ec55d5ac7a8))\n- save local terminals as connections: the connection dialog saves a local terminal with its shell, a start directory (typed or picked, ~ for home), startup commands typed in each time the shell starts, a terminal theme, a highlight set, a logging choice and a group, and lists it in the launcher, the hosts panel and their search; a local tab without a profile can be saved from its menu or with Mod+Shift+O, which opens the dialog filled with its shell, the directory it is in and its name, and edits the saved connection of a tab that has one; a saved tab keeps running in the directory it is in when the profile is saved or edited, and deleting the profile leaves its local tabs open, unsaved; a connection's own terminal theme now applies to every kind of tab, where only SSH tabs used it and a serial profile's theme was ignored ([0d26b365](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/0d26b365fad704d88c273678345c6ddea2afef41))\n- let a saved profile be a local terminal, keeping the shell it starts (by kind, path, the user's own shell id or WSL distribution) and the directory it starts in, so a local tab that was set up for a task can be saved and opened there again; a start directory may begin with ~, which is the home directory of the machine it opens on, for local shells and WSL alike, so the same profile works on devices whose home directories differ ([728515cd](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/728515cd92c4be77fd225e05ea66a78126b515d5))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.8.0...v0.8.1-beta.1](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.8.0...v0.8.1-beta.1)",
